  ('fandom-heroes', 'Marvel Rivals Fandom Heroes', 'https://marvelrivals.fandom.com/api.php?action=query&list=categorymembers&cmtitle=Category:Heroes', '{"synced":["Adam Warlock","Angela","Black Cat","Black Panther","Black Widow","Blade","Captain America","Cloak & Dagger","Cyclops","Daredevil","Deadpool","Devil Dinosaur","Doctor Strange","Elsa Bloodstone","Emma Frost","Gambit","Groot","Hawkeye","Hela","Hulk","Human Torch","Invisible Woman","Iron Fist","Iron Man","Jeff the Land Shark","Loki","Luna Snow","Magik","Magneto","Mantis","Mister Fantastic","Moon Knight","Namor","Peni Parker","Phoenix","Psylocke","Rocket Raccoon","Rogue","Scarlet Witch","Spider-Man","Squirrel Girl","Star-Lord","Storm","The Punisher","The Thing","Thor","Ultron","Venom","White Fox","Winter Soldier","Wolverine"],"skipped":["Moon Girl"],"heroPages":[{"pageid":215,"ns":0,"title":"Adam Warlock"},{"pageid":982,"ns":0,"title":"Angela"},{"pageid":29060,"ns":0,"title":"Black Cat"},{"pageid":193,"ns":0,"title":"Black Panther"},{"pageid":835,"ns":0,"title":"Black Widow"},{"pageid":971,"ns":0,"title":"Blade"},{"pageid":392,"ns":0,"title":"Captain America"},{"pageid":938,"ns":0,"title":"Cloak & Dagger"},{"pageid":1996,"ns":0,"title":"Cyclops"},{"pageid":16504,"ns":0,"title":"Daredevil"},{"pageid":932,"ns":0,"title":"Deadpool"},{"pageid":34899,"ns":0,"title":"Devil Dinosaur"},{"pageid":196,"ns":0,"title":"Doctor Strange"},{"pageid":25506,"ns":0,"title":"Elsa Bloodstone"},{"pageid":1109,"ns":0,"title":"Emma Frost"},{"pageid":19124,"ns":0,"title":"Gambit"},{"pageid":203,"ns":0,"title":"Groot"},{"pageid":915,"ns":0,"title":"Hawkeye"},{"pageid":217,"ns":0,"title":"Hela"},{"pageid":195,"ns":0,"title":"Hulk"},{"pageid":964,"ns":0,"title":"Human Torch"},{"pageid":963,"ns":0,"title":"Invisible Woman"},{"pageid":939,"ns":0,"title":"Iron Fist"},{"pageid":192,"ns":0,"title":"Iron Man"},{"pageid":266,"ns":0,"title":"Jeff the Land Shark"},{"pageid":197,"ns":0,"title":"Loki"},{"pageid":199,"ns":0,"title":"Luna Snow"},{"pageid":200,"ns":0,"title":"Magik"},{"pageid":218,"ns":0,"title":"Magneto"},{"pageid":222,"ns":0,"title":"Mantis"},{"pageid":958,"ns":0,"title":"Mister Fantastic"},{"pageid":42466,"ns":0,"title":"Moon Girl"},{"pageid":866,"ns":0,"title":"Moon Knight"},{"pageid":202,"ns":0,"title":"Namor"},{"pageid":198,"ns":0,"title":"Peni Parker"},{"pageid":1025,"ns":0,"title":"Phoenix"},{"pageid":411,"ns":0,"title":"Psylocke"},{"pageid":201,"ns":0,"title":"Rocket Raccoon"},{"pageid":19123,"ns":0,"title":"Rogue"},{"pageid":224,"ns":0,"title":"Scarlet Witch"},{"pageid":194,"ns":0,"title":"Spider-Man"},{"pageid":940,"ns":0,"title":"Squirrel Girl"},{"pageid":216,"ns":0,"title":"Star-Lord"},{"pageid":221,"ns":0,"title":"Storm"},{"pageid":241,"ns":0,"title":"The Punisher"},{"pageid":965,"ns":0,"title":"The Thing"},{"pageid":265,"ns":0,"title":"Thor"},{"pageid":968,"ns":0,"title":"Ultron"},{"pageid":214,"ns":0,"title":"Venom"},{"pageid":18299,"ns":0,"title":"White Fox"},{"pageid":494,"ns":0,"title":"Winter Soldier"},{"pageid":931,"ns":0,"title":"Wolverine"}]}'::jsonb, '2026-07-04T05:10:46.444Z', 'success', null),
  ('nerfpool-s9-week1', 'Nerfpool: Every Hero''s Win Rate (Season 9, Week 1)', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VB6OIA-ChmA', '{"videoId":"VB6OIA-ChmA","title":"Nerfpool: Every Hero''s Win Rate (Season 9, Week 1)","sourceUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VB6OIA-ChmA","season":9,"week":1,"transcript":"Intro\r\n0:00\r\nWelcome to the very first episode of the Nerf Dict, the actual site of the Marvel Rivals\r\n0:06\r\nmeta by the numbers for the ranks that you actually play in. I''ll be posting a video just like this one every Friday to\r\n0:13\r\nkeep your pretty face updated. Timestamps are below. Feel free to jump to whatever topic you care about. It''s\r\n0:21\r\nokay. You can totally butcher my video engagement. I don''t mind.\r\nVANGUARD WIN RATES\r\n0:26\r\nThe very first tank we''ll be covering is Penny Parker. And [laughter] holy crap,\r\nPeni Parker\r\n0:31\r\nPenny, what have you been smoking? Easily the best tank in the game. And it''s not even close. I mean, look at\r\n0:39\r\nthat curve. She''s already at 58% in the low ranks. And she just keeps on\r\n0:45\r\nclimbing to 60, 63, 65, all the way to 66% in Grandmaster before settling\r\n0:52\r\ncomfortably at 64% in Celestial. Now, here''s the thing. Lowo hands are free\r\n0:57\r\nwins because Lowo does not understand that deployables are destroyable and\r\n1:03\r\ndoes not understand the concept of zoning. They simply can''t understand the simple problems that she puts on the\r\n1:09\r\nfloor. So, she is printing money. However, you would expect her win rate to just plummet once she climbs up top.\r\n1:16\r\nExcept it doesn''t. Even at the high top, people are still struggling against her,\r\n1:22\r\nespecially now with the rocket team up and the fact that she can get multiple nests up. That essentially multiplies\r\n1:28\r\nthe zoning problem, which is enormous value for her whole team. Of course, if you take the nests out on a consistent\r\n1:34\r\nbasis, she is practically useless. The alt is pretty good, but for whatever reason, people seem to be struggling.\r\n1:39\r\nSo, if you want to play a great tank this season, go for Penny. Next up, we have The Thing. And he looks pretty\r\nThe Thing\r\n1:46\r\ndecent early on. 54 to 56% across the low ranks. And then he quietly bleeds\r\n1:52\r\nout on the side of a streak the higher you go. Down to 52% in Grandmaster and 50% in celestial. See that right there\r\n2:00\r\nis the signature of a hero that the top ranks know exactly how to punish and the bottom ranks don''t. See, Lowo doesn''t\r\n2:06\r\nreally take those opportunities. Then they also can''t aim well enough even though he''s a big giant orange rock. If\r\n2:13\r\nyou''re playing Thing in Diamond and Platinum the way you want to play him in celestial, you''re going to explode. You\r\n2:19\r\ngot the same hero here, but one end knows exactly how to play him and the other one doesn''t. And trust me, as you\r\n2:25\r\nkeep watching, this will continue to be a pattern. Next up, we have Thor. And he\r\nThor\r\n2:31\r\nhas the most snoozefest lineup of anybody here. And that''s not a bad\r\n2:37\r\nthing. He is basically at a flat 53% from the low ranks all up to celestial.\r\n2:42\r\nAnd honestly, I''m not really surprised because his new teamups give him a lot more survivability, which used to be his\r\n2:48\r\nbiggest problem. What''s really interesting is that this off tank, you know, the kind of tank that used to\r\n2:55\r\nexplode on site before is now outperforming the shield main tanks that everybody is crying about all the time.\r\nHulk\r\n3:01\r\nNext up, we have the Hulk. And he is fairly steady at around 52 through the low to mid ranks and basically the same\r\n3:09\r\nup top, 52% in GM, 51% in Celestial. I''d be really curious to see at some point,\r\n3:16\r\neven though the data is probably not going to be amazing, whether the higher ranks above that, which is Eternity and\r\n3:21\r\nOne Above All, are going to do better with Hulk. I know that he is a character that has a lot of complexity to him. And\r\n3:27\r\nbased on what I''m seeing here, regardless of the new teamups, regardless of the Wolverine teamup, that\r\n3:32\r\nmakes him, I would assume, a lot easier to play because he just does the punching faster and it does more damage.\r\n3:39\r\nStill, the win rate''s not where it needs to be. He is a great pick right now, but other dive tanks like Venom seem to be\r\n3:45\r\nperforming a lot better as you''re going to see. Next up, we have Groot. And Groot is the perfect example of it''s not\r\nGroot\r\n3:53\r\nthe plane, it''s the pilot. See, down in the low ranks, they completely misuse\r\n3:58\r\nthat giant ficus. They just turn them into bits. Low ranks think that tanking\r\n4:04\r\nis taking damage and pressing W, and that is incorrect. They don''t wall\r\n4:09\r\nanyone off. They don''t understand how to zone. They typically whiff or misuse the\r\n4:14\r\nalt. And god forbid they ever combine their alts with someone else and well,\r\n4:19\r\ncommunicated. So, you got these measly win rates of 50%, 52%, 53%, up until\r\n4:26\r\ncelestial. And then celestial spikes up at 58%. Because the high ranks know exactly how\r\n4:33\r\nto be a Groot and their teammates also know how to follow up to a Groot. As far\r\n4:38\r\nas I can see, the low ranks have no idea how to play Groot and the higher ranks are going, \"Watch this, bro. Hold my\r\n4:45\r\nfertilizer.\" Next up, we have Angela. Now, watch that curve climb, hovering\r\nAngela\r\n4:51\r\n50% to 53% in the low ranks and then spiking to a delicious 57% in celestial.\r\n4:58\r\nThat is for a few reasons. First of all, she is a hyper mobile off tank, which means that she demands a lot more\r\n5:04\r\ncreativity and game sense that low elo just doesn''t have. Also, she is not a\r\n5:09\r\nstat farmer. You''re not going to see an Angela with tons of damage done or tons of block damage as well. Her whole value\r\n5:16\r\nis all around displacement of individual enemies, typically tanks, and also shutting down flankers and winning 1v\r\n5:23\r\nons. Unfortunately, low elo doesn''t give her any of those really rich\r\n5:28\r\nopportunities because no one at low elo is going to flank in a really inspired way. No, they''re just going to be a\r\n5:34\r\nStar-Lord or a Psylo and stand behind their tanks and pump damage down main. And with this placement, forget about\r\n5:41\r\nit. Do you know how many times I would be Angela and push a Magneto deep into our team and then our team would just\r\n5:48\r\ngo, \"H, look [laughter] at that. That''s crazy.\" Anyway, pew pew. Now, Highlo is\r\n5:53\r\nthe opposite. They know exactly what she''s setting up. They know exactly what her role is and they know how to capitalize on her. If she pushes a tank\r\n6:00\r\ninto their lines, they delete it. If she sees a really aggressive flank, she stops it, which allows your flankers to\r\n6:06\r\ndo whatever the hell they want. In many ways, she is manufacturing team fight wins and shutting down the winning\r\n6:13\r\ncondition of the other team, which is why Higher ELO is much better as her. Next up, we have poor old Magneto. What\r\nMagneto\r\n6:20\r\nhappened, man? Flat 50 to 52% the entire way. Low ranks, high ranks, it doesn''t\r\n6:28\r\nmatter. He has always been a comfort pick. But one of the big issues with Magneto for the past few seasons is that\r\n6:34\r\nhe really doesn''t have a lot of agency and a lot of impact. Yes, I know when you alt correctly, you can put your big\r\n6:41\r\ngiant meatball on top of a cloak and dagger''s forehead. That''s useful, but other than that, in the neutral, what is\r\n6:48\r\nhe doing? It''s ridiculous because his kit is extremely useful. There is value\r\n6:54\r\nin having a big chunky thick boy at the front. But a lot of times as Magneto,\r\n6:59\r\nespecially in the low to mid ranks, you''d be bubbling people, which on paper is huge value, but those people end up\r\n7:05\r\ndying anyway because the reason you had to bubble them in the first place is because of their positioning, which doesn''t magically improve when you\r\n7:12\r\nbubble them. Frustration. For now, he just seems to sit in the front and do\r\n7:18\r\nhis thing and sometimes win and sometimes not. Next up, we have Venom. Now he is dead even at 50% through the\r\nVenom\r\n7:26\r\nlow ranks, then climbs up a little bit to 53% in Grandmaster and then 57% in\r\n7:32\r\nCelestial. This is another classic story of low elo has no idea what to do with him, and then high elo is [ __ ]\r\n7:38\r\ncooking. At low elo, it''s pretty basic. They''ll just swing in at random times,\r\n7:44\r\nmiss all their shots, have terrible target priority, and then wait for the swing out cooldown to appear, pop their\r\n7:52\r\nextra health, and either die or don''t die. But ultimately, they don''t create any pressure. They also don''t know how\r\n7:57\r\nto use the alt, and of course, their team is not going to follow up on that alt. They''re just going to look and\r\n8:02\r\nwatch from afar and wait for him to kill the whole team, which is not going to happen. And then at high elo, they have\r\n8:08\r\ntiming. They understand the basic concepts of diving and they know how to apply those to Venom. They also know how\r\n8:14\r\nto get the most out of his new team up with Phoenix, which is awesome. Their target priority is on point. They''re\r\n8:20\r\ntracking the cooldowns and the ultimates of the enemy team. They know when to hard engage versus when to soften\r\n8:26\r\nengage. And one of the things that really good venoms do is that when they need to exit, they understand the\r\n8:31\r\ngeometry around them. A lot of them are going to climb up a wall or run up a wall rather and then use their slam cool\r\n8:37\r\ndown which typically is going to be back before the swing to go back to their team and get out of dodge. This is\r\n8:44\r\nanother example of it''s not the plane, it''s definitely the pilot. Next up, we\r\nCaptain America\r\n8:49\r\nhave my boy Captain America. And this one genuinely surprises me. He is 49 to\r\n8:54\r\n52% through the low ranks and basically stuck at 50% in Grandmaster and Celestial. And that flat line tells me\r\n9:01\r\nsomething''s really off. Mostly because as a cap one trick, I am eating good. I\r\n9:07\r\nrun around 60% win rate on him and the new teamups turn me from just a annoying\r\n9:13\r\nmosquito to someone that can suck some blood. But for whatever reason, everyone\r\n9:18\r\nexcept maybe people in Eternity and One Above All. It''s interesting because someone like\r\n9:24\r\nVenom does spike in win rate, but someone like Cap doesn''t. And I wonder if that''s because of the more violent\r\n9:30\r\nnature of a Venom as a dive tank versus Cap who has more peel potential. His\r\n9:36\r\nultimate is a support ultimate and not an aggressive ultimate. I don''t know where it''s coming from, but I kind of\r\n9:41\r\nlike it. Don''t don''t get that, you know, win rate really high up. [laughter] I want me some buffs. Next up, we have\r\nDevil Dinosaur\r\n9:47\r\nDevil Dinosaur. And my god, what a big red wamp wamp. 47% to 50% in the low\r\n9:55\r\nranks and then sinking to a stinky 46% in celestial. My god. Yeah, buddy. You\r\n10:02\r\nare extinct, huh? See, there''s a clear pattern in this game. If you''re a bulky frontline body that just stands there,\r\n10:10\r\nyou pop. At low elo, he just takes damage and dies. And the weird thing about him is that he also hogs the\r\n10:17\r\nheals. For whatever reason, supports in low ilo are obsessed with keeping people\r\n10:22\r\nalive in a very sloppy way. So when he is low on health, he really needs a lot\r\n10:27\r\nof help not to die. But that hogs the healing. So if anyone else needs some healing at that time, well, you''re [ __ ]\r\n10:33\r\nout of luck. Meanwhile, celestial dino players are clearly still hunting for a\r\n10:39\r\nplay style that works post the nerfs. His teamups are not too great, and he is a little bit in La La Land. Next up, we\r\nRogue\r\n10:46\r\nhave Rogue. And she is a big fat meh at the bottom. 45% to 49% through the low\r\n10:52\r\nranks, which doesn''t really surprise me at all because low ELO doesn''t really want a character with depth that demands\r\n11:00\r\ntiming and purpose. No, they just they just want to autopilot, man. And you have to be genuinely skilled to even\r\n11:07\r\nunderstand the problems that Rogue solves and the problems that she can create. Later on, she climbs a little\r\n11:13\r\nbit. 51% in GM and 52% in celestial. And as better players figure out how to\r\n11:19\r\nsqueeze value out of her, things do improve a little bit, but she''s definitely reliable. The top ranks\r\n11:25\r\nclearly understand her and her alt timing better, and they also understand that she absolutely rewards alt and\r\n11:32\r\nability tracking. But here we go again. You''re going to keep seeing it, and you have been seeing it. It''s the recurring\r\n11:38\r\ntheme in this whole video. Heroes that require actual thinking sag at the\r\n11:43\r\nbottom and climb toward the top. Next up, we have Emma Frost. Now, this is\r\nEmma Frost\r\n11:48\r\nrough basically everywhere. She''s one of the few and maybe the only tank that\r\n11:54\r\ndoesn''t really tip over 50% or even lick it [laughter] at all in this list. I couldn''t tell you\r\n12:01\r\nwhy. I''ve had a lot of success with Emma. I feel like Emma''s do pose problems at my rank. So, I''m wondering\r\n12:08\r\nwhether this is potentially a data issue, but probably not given the accuracy of these trackers versus the\r\n12:15\r\nofficial data. I don''t know why. It could be that a lot of people are letting her solo tank, which doesn''t\r\n12:20\r\nmake a lot of sense given that she''s an anchor tank and she absolutely needs some help. In any case, this one doesn''t\r\n12:26\r\nalign with reality for me, but I''ll trust it for now and wait for more data to come out and see if this improves in\r\n12:31\r\nthe weeks that are coming. Next up, we have Doctor Strange, or should I say Dr. normal. He is one of the worst tanks in\r\nDoctor Strange\r\n12:39\r\nthe game by win rate alone. This is 46 to 48% in low elo, then slides to 45% in\r\n12:45\r\ncelestial. And my god, another one that surprises me enough that I''m thinking, is this a data artifact? Again, I''ve\r\n12:53\r\ncompared Strange''s win rate between trackers and official sources, and it seems right. But I just wonder whether\r\n12:59\r\nhim being used for a teleport is somehow skewing his numbers cuz Strange is great\r\n13:05\r\nthis season. His team ups are powerful. The Gamma one is really great. He packs a bigger punch. He is very useful. I\r\n13:12\r\njust don''t get it. What is interesting to me is that the big chunky tanks of Magneto and Doctor Strange that\r\n13:18\r\neverybody is crying about whenever you''re running two tanks that are off tanking and anchoring together are\r\n13:24\r\nactually not doing that great. And I will tell you, for Magneto specifically, who I play a lot more, I feel it. And\r\n13:30\r\nmaybe the strange players can tell me in the comments whether they''re feeling this as well, but my god, this doesn''t\r\nTankpool\r\n13:36\r\nlook good. And finally, we have tankpool. And my god, arguably one of\r\n13:42\r\nthe worst performing tanks right now, especially at the bottom. A genuinely\r\n13:47\r\ngrim 42% in silver, sitting in the mid-40s across Lowo in general. My read\r\n13:53\r\nis Lillo loves to die constantly and a lot of his value is tied to his ultimate\r\n13:59\r\nwhich resets when he dies. So not only are they not using their ultimate as much, I really doubt that they know when\r\n14:06\r\nto use it and how to use it. And I know for a fact that their team is not following up, but then if that was true,\r\n14:13\r\nyou would think that GM and Celestial figured it out a little bit. And in a way they did. There is a lot of depth\r\n14:19\r\nand nuance to the character who is genuinely very good. It''s just that these ranks for whatever reason have no\r\n14:26\r\nidea how to pilot this guy. Now, moving on to the healers or\r\nSTRATEGIST WIN RATES\r\n14:32\r\nstrategists if you want to be correct though. First up, we have Mantis and handsdown the queen of the supports\r\nMantis\r\n14:40\r\nright now. And it''s not even a competition. Already 59 to 63% across the low ranks and climbing to 63% in GM.\r\n14:47\r\nand then all the way to 66% in celestial. My god, girl. And the fact\r\n14:54\r\nthat she climbs tells you that her ceiling is probably all about the trigger finger. She does real damage.\r\n15:01\r\nSo, in the low ranks, she''s already a menace just on raw value. Especially now that with her new teamups, she can just\r\n15:07\r\nwork in a double support and she does AOE healing and a lot of burst healing. It''s beautiful. And then up top in the\r\n15:14\r\nhands of somebody that can actually hit their shots and more specifically hit their head shot. She is an additional\r\n15:19\r\nDPS who happens to heal a whole lot. And let''s not forget that she also boosts\r\n15:25\r\nher team. So that''s also quite useful. Right now there''s no rank where she''s not performing amazingly. And the better\r\n15:32\r\nthe player, the more terrifying that she gets. If you can aim, this is the highest value hero in the entire game.\r\nUltron\r\n15:39\r\nNext up, we have Ultron. Now, our favorite tin can is really good in low to mid-ranks. 58 to 61% and then does a\r\n15:48\r\nslight cool down up top to 56% in GM and 57% in celestial. That shape makes a lot\r\n15:55\r\nof sense to me. Flyers are just more punishable the more you go up the rank, so that''s fine. In any case, he is still\r\n16:02\r\nexcellent everywhere. The alt has a lot of value as well. The low to mid ranks seem to be eating good right now, mostly\r\n16:09\r\nbecause there''s an aiming problem and he can just get away with a lot of things that he can''t get away at GM and celestial. So, if you''re grinding out\r\n16:16\r\ngold, he is a very, very good option to just get free wins. Next up, we have\r\nRocket Raccoon\r\n16:22\r\nRocket Raccoon. Now, the rat is basically a metronome. 56 to 58% in the\r\n16:28\r\nlow ranks, 57% in GM, 55% in celestial. Damn, he''s reliable at every single\r\n16:35\r\nlevel. This is probably the most consistent main healer in the entire game. And consistency at every rank\r\n16:42\r\nmeans the hero doesn''t ask much of you beyond just doing your freaking job. He absolutely thrives when your team has\r\n16:48\r\ndiversitive is really big this season. So, there you go. By far, he is the safest support to\r\n16:55\r\npick on the board. And I hope that the stigma around him being really simple to play starts to disappear. The character\r\n17:02\r\nis more complex than people think and he is just awesome. Next up we have Adam Warlock and he has a bit of a jagged\r\nAdam Warlock\r\n17:09\r\nline. He is a big 58% in silver. Then he dips to 50% through the middle and then\r\n17:15\r\nclimbs right back up to 55% in celestial. Basically when the team suits his burst he pops. And when it doesn''t,\r\n17:23\r\nhe''s just kind of a middling 40s to 50% filler kind of character. The silver\r\n17:28\r\nspike is just probably newish players overvaluing the res. And then the\r\n17:34\r\ncelestial climb is just good players building around his kit very intentionally. I would say for him, read\r\n17:40\r\nthe room before you lock him and see how much of a commitment you want to make. He is great, but there are much better\r\nLoki\r\n17:46\r\noptions. Next up, we have Loki. And I''m very happy to see that he is a very clean climber. 49% to 53% in the low\r\n17:54\r\nranks and then up to 55% in GM and finally 57% in celestial. He is a\r\n18:00\r\nflexible healer, one of the most flexible healers, and flexibility only pays off if you know when to use it and\r\n18:06\r\nhow to use it. Unfortunately, low elo doesn''t. So there he ends up being a bit more of a coin flip. They just put\r\n18:13\r\nclones in random places. They misuse their lamp. It''s just a [ __ ] show. But then the more you rise up the rank and\r\n18:19\r\nthe intelligence and skill of the players improves as well, his kit which should be used very purposely is used\r\n18:27\r\nvery purposely and then he becomes very good. Next up we have cloak and dagger.\r\nCloak & Dagger\r\n18:33\r\nYeah, she is winning the popularity contest and quietly sinking the higher\r\n18:38\r\nyou go. 48% to 50% in the low ranks and then slides to 46% in GM and a very very\r\n18:45\r\nrough 43% in celestial. It''s interesting because she is the inverse of a skill\r\n18:51\r\nexpressive hero. Her kit is forgiving enough to feel fine when nobody''s punishing your mistakes and then the\r\n18:57\r\nmoment you hit the ranks where they do punish the whole thing falls apart. Low elo loves her because she''s just\r\n19:04\r\ncomfortable and high elo exposes exactly what that comfort is hiding which is lack of skill. Next up we have invisible\r\nInvisible Woman\r\n19:12\r\nwoman. Now she is a flat unremarkable 46 to 47% in the low ranks then goes up to\r\n19:18\r\n48% in GM and then 46% in celestial. There''s genuinely not much of a story\r\n19:24\r\nhere. She''s just a main healer who never single-handedly loses or wins you a game\r\n19:29\r\nat any rank. She is very good, very reliable. There''s no skill floor here that really saves her, but there''s also\r\n19:36\r\nno skill ceiling that extremely rewards you. She does the job in a reliable way.\r\n19:41\r\nShe passes the grade and then that''s about it. So, perfectly playable,\r\n19:47\r\nquietly below average everywhere. Next up, we have White Fox. Now, she''s a main\r\nWhite Fox\r\n19:53\r\nhealer whose line sinks as you climb, and we keep seeing that over and over again. 46 to 47% in the low ranks and\r\n20:00\r\nthen drops to 43% in GM and 42% in celestial. I think this is the same\r\n20:05\r\nstory as cloak and dagger man. Her specific weaknesses simply don''t get punished enough in low elo and then get\r\n20:13\r\nruthlessly punished once the players know how. So, if you are someone in the lower ELO that wants to completely break\r\n20:19\r\nthe legs off of another team, figure out what celestial and grandmaster players do to the white foxes there and then\r\n20:26\r\napply it back down in the low elo and win yourself some games. Facts are that when a support falls off this cleanly\r\n20:33\r\nand this hard towards the top, it''s almost always because the kit has an exploit that the good players have\r\n20:39\r\nfigured out and the average players haven''t. Next up, we have Jeffy. Now, he\r\nJeff the Land Shark\r\n20:44\r\nis fairly middling right now with mid-rank bumps. So, he is 44 to 49%\r\n20:50\r\nthrough low elo and then 49% in GM and then back down to 46% in celestial. So,\r\n20:56\r\nit''s not great. I think generally speaking, Jeffs are spotty and a lot of\r\n21:02\r\npeople play them for various reasons. It''s very rare to see a really good Jeff that understands how to Jeff it up. Many\r\n21:09\r\nmany people struggle to get true value out of the alt and you can see that that''s represented. He''s a great\r\n21:14\r\ncharacter and at the higher elo he''s completely overpowered but then up until celestial as you can see it''s just not\r\nGambit\r\n21:21\r\ngood. Next up we have Gambit and this one is interesting. He is one of the biggest clims on the entire board. He\r\n21:29\r\nstarts off at a very forgettable 45 to 48% in the low ranks and then 51% in GM\r\n21:35\r\nand then a huge spike to 57% in celestial. This is definitely a hero\r\n21:40\r\nthat the low ranks have not figured out and we know that he is busted. We know that he is instab in many lobbies up\r\n21:47\r\ntop. Low rank has no idea what to do with him. I am not really surprised. You can see a pattern here, which is really\r\n21:53\r\ninteresting. And I''m sure as more episodes of this show come out, we''re going to be seeing this over and over\r\n21:58\r\nagain. And I''m going to start sounding like a busted, broken record very quickly. Any character at low elo that\r\n22:04\r\nrequires team synergy and you guys pushing all together and communicating\r\n22:10\r\nand doing stuff in a synchronized way fails. his ultimate needs to be used in\r\n22:15\r\na very efficient, pushy, bully kind of way because you can practically do\r\n22:20\r\nanything you want during it. But then for most people, they just do what they do. And I''ve seen Gambit alt on a bunch\r\n22:26\r\nof people and they just stand on cart and shoot from afar and it''s just so disheartening to see. So I don''t think\r\n22:32\r\nthis win rate, these numbers are a representation of the quality of the character. It''s just again quality of\r\n22:38\r\nthe teams and quality of the pilots in many cases. Next up, we have the new girl on the block, and that''s Jubilee.\r\nJubilee\r\n22:45\r\nNot great. She''s brand new this season. It''s what, week oneish. People are still\r\n22:51\r\nfiguring out the kit. She''s a flat 45 to 47% in low ELO and then then it pretty\r\n22:57\r\nmuch stays like that up until Celestial. I''m really curious to see how this data shifts in the coming weeks. Watch next\r\n23:03\r\nepisode and the one after to see if there''s any variance here. But right now, the way that it feels is she''s\r\n23:09\r\npretty stable, right? She''s not busted, which is pretty rare for new hero releases these days. The only problem I\r\n23:16\r\nhave with her is all the visual clutter. I mean, my lord, this game was just an\r\n23:21\r\noverstimulating mess before, and now I need to take a cigarette break and go on\r\n23:27\r\nthe balcony and relax and breathe for 10 minutes every time she als. Next up, we have Luna Snow. Me. Flat mid40s the\r\nLuna Snow\r\n23:35\r\nwhole way. a 45 to 47% in the low ranks and then 47% in GM and 46% in celestial.\r\n23:41\r\nDo not let these stats stop you from playing her. The fact that she has a way to cleanse herself off of any stuns\r\n23:49\r\nwhile being stunned is [ __ ] ridiculous. But the reality is there''s\r\n23:55\r\nno ELO right now where she is the answer to anything. And there''s no ILO where she''s a complete disaster either. And\r\n24:01\r\nfinally, we have heelpool. Oh my god, what''s happening with the Deadpools? The\r\nHealpool\r\n24:06\r\nworst support in the game at almost every rank. Mid40s through low elo and\r\n24:13\r\nthen cratering down to 41% in celestial. What the [ __ ] you guys? Again, a\r\n24:20\r\ncharacter with real depth and real nuance that needs to stay alive. And these [ __ ] are dying left and\r\n24:26\r\nright. Learn how to have uptime.\r\n24:32\r\nOh boy. Let''s talk about the DPS players. First up, we got Storm, the\r\nStorm\r\n24:37\r\nbronze queen. 56 to 58% in the low ranks. I wonder why. Oh yeah, nobody can\r\n24:45\r\nlook up and shoot at her. Then she gently fades to 55% in GM and then 54%\r\n24:51\r\nand Celestial. This is pretty good performance. You know, the most important thing here is that we have a\r\n24:56\r\nseason now where Storm is comfortably over 50% which tells me that she can climb very well. And who knows, maybe\r\n25:04\r\nNet Ease is going to give her a [ __ ] skin at some point. Next up, we have\r\nMagik\r\n25:09\r\nMagic. The most consistent DPS in the entire game. Full stop. 54 to 58%\r\n25:17\r\nthrough the low ranks. 55% win rate in GM and back to 57% in Celestial.\r\n25:24\r\nFeel the burn. She is very flexible right now and she''s got all her cool\r\n25:30\r\nteamups. I think there''s a lot of potential in the one that she has with the hood that people are still yet to\r\n25:36\r\nuncover. She can be at the front with a solo tank, do a fair bit of damage, get her health up, and then portal to the\r\n25:41\r\nbackline and do some damage. She can completely play as a flanker and a diver as well. And my god, can she kill? That\r\n25:48\r\nis rare. She is not a hero that spikes at the top and then murkies the waters\r\n25:53\r\nat the bottom. Absolutely not. She is just good everywhere at every single\r\n25:59\r\nlevel. and that is very rare for DPS characters. Next up, we have Iron Man.\r\nIron Man\r\n26:05\r\nHe is very strong at every rank except one brutal cliff. 52 to 56% through the\r\n26:11\r\nlow ranks, 54% in GM, and then a stunning collapse to 44% in celestial.\r\n26:19\r\nYeah, I guess people can aim. They''re low to the ground. They''re corner peaking. They only flank when they''re\r\n26:25\r\nabout to alt. But the lore, that drop is entirely a playstyle story. The big\r\n26:31\r\ninteresting movement in the Iron Man fandom club thing, whatever, has been\r\n26:37\r\nthat more and more really good Iron Men are not playing him up in the air. No,\r\n26:42\r\nthey''re playing him like Storm, very close to the ground. Obviously, low ELO will never learn how to look up and aim\r\n26:49\r\nat something or, god forbid, they''re not going to switch characters to counter the Iron Man, so he can do whatever he\r\n26:54\r\nwants there. But then in higher elo, these people can aim and they will punish that play style that we''re all\r\n27:00\r\nvery familiar with. The really good Iron Man are playing him nice and low right behind their tanks right in front of the\r\n27:07\r\nhealers. So they, you know, bypass the entire problem with him getting healed and he can still hit his shots and they\r\n27:13\r\nbasically play him like a hella. It could be that that play style has been adopted way more into Eternity and One\r\n27:19\r\nAbove All, but Celestial already is punishing this dude. I''m really curious to see whether the Iron Men there have\r\n27:26\r\nfigured out a way to play him or if it''s just brutalism all the way. Next up, we have Psylock. And she is a clean, easy\r\nPsylocke\r\n27:33\r\nclimbber. 51 to 56% through the low ranks and then peaks at 57% win rate in\r\n27:38\r\nGM before easing into 54% at Celestial. Psylock is a pure flanker and in many\r\n27:45\r\nways she''s an alt merchant, very, very similar to Star-Lord. Being able to flank correctly and position and survive\r\n27:52\r\nand have target priority rewards you the higher you climb. Lowo can''t really use\r\n27:57\r\nher. Although if you just form your ult and pop it at the right time, that is a lot of value. And then high ranks love\r\n28:05\r\nher. The tiny celestial dip is interesting. It''s probably the very best players having the awareness to answer a\r\n28:12\r\nflank and maybe the, you know, the Angelas I was talking about before with the really high win rates would easily\r\n28:18\r\nshut down a Psylock. So, that''s an interesting matchup. But everywhere from gold to GM, she is a problem. Next up,\r\nMister Fantastic\r\n28:25\r\nwe have Mr. Fantastic. And it''s only fair that he is a bouncy boy. And his\r\n28:32\r\nwin rate is also quite bouncy up and down, too. He lands pretty strong, though. 51 to 57% through low elo and\r\n28:39\r\nthen a 49% dip in GM and then back up to 54% in celestial. You see, heroes whose\r\n28:45\r\nvalue is largely situational always tend to produce jagged charts like this. So\r\n28:50\r\nthat''s fine, mostly because their impact just depends on whether the game hands them the moment that they''re really\r\n28:57\r\nbuilt for. And with him specifically, a lot of his value is tied to his ult as well. His neutral is great, but the alt\r\n29:03\r\ncan be very powerful, but you need the right geometry for that to happen. However, don''t let the noise fool you.\r\n29:10\r\nHe is incredibly fun. He ends strong at the top for a reason, which tells you\r\n29:15\r\nthat the good players have figured out something that low elo hasn''t. Next up, we have Daredevil. This is your textbook\r\nDaredevil\r\n29:22\r\ndiver climb. 50 to 54% of the low ranks. You know, they''re figuring out the combos, figuring out what their mouse\r\n29:29\r\ndoes. then 57% in celestial. How interesting. You see, pure dive rewards\r\n29:35\r\nmechanics and timing and game sense, which is why the line rises so cleanly\r\n29:41\r\nwith the rank. The better you can hit your shots and your combos and pick your moment and pick your targets, the more\r\n29:48\r\nyour hero gives back. Those heroes are also useless in the hands of people they\r\n29:53\r\ncan''t execute, and they''re terrifying in the hands of people they can. Next up, we have Black Cat. And [laughter]\r\nBlack Cat\r\n30:01\r\none of the biggest climbs in the entire game, maybe the biggest this week, 49 to\r\n30:06\r\nabout 55% through the low ranks, then jumps to 56% in GM in a chart topping\r\n30:13\r\n59% in Celestial, baby. That also happens, by the way, to\r\n30:20\r\nbe the best DPS number up there. She scales almost perfectly with player\r\n30:25\r\nskill, and that''s really awesome to see because she does have a lot of player expression, and she did always feel like\r\n30:31\r\nthe kind of character that rewards you. In the low ranks, she''s kind of a throw\r\n30:36\r\npick and maybe a coin flip at best. And then at the top, she is the best carry in the game, bar none. Next up, we have\r\nIron Fist\r\n30:44\r\nIron Fist. Flat low 50s, no drama, no big deal. 51 to 54% of the low ranks.\r\n30:51\r\n51% in GM and 52% in Celestial. Me, he''s gonna be at the front. He''s gonna brawl\r\n30:57\r\nwith the occasional dive mixed in, but I don''t know if Iron Fist players have\r\n31:03\r\nfound his identity yet, and I actually don''t know that Net Ease has found his identity yet. If I had to do a tier list\r\n31:09\r\nhere, he''s probably a solid B+ at every rank. He is rarely a bad pick, but also\r\n31:15\r\nthere''s so many better ones. So, should you pick him? I don''t know. He''s reliable. He is not highly complicated\r\n31:21\r\nand quietly fine. Next up, we have Hela. Now, again, speaking of reliability, low\r\nHela\r\n31:28\r\n50s that barely moves in the low ranks, then 51 to 54% through the midling\r\n31:34\r\nranks, 52% in GM, and then 54% in celestial. It does help that she carries\r\n31:40\r\nsome of the most useful, you know, teamups out there. So, that''s good. But, in the end, she is part of the entire,\r\n31:46\r\nyou know, poke slop phase. then you just sit behind your tank, sit in front of your healers, take a little bit of\r\n31:52\r\ncover, and then shoot people. And your mechanics are either going to carry you from that point on or not. So, if you\r\n31:58\r\njust want to click on people''s heads, fine. She is a safe, dependable pick at literally every level of the rank so\r\n32:05\r\nfar. And she''s also boring in kind of the best way ever. Next up, we have Black Panther. And this one, this one\r\nBlack Panther\r\n32:12\r\nmakes sense. He is great at the bottom, but then falls off a cliff at the top.\r\n32:18\r\nWe have 51 to 56% win rate through the low ranks. Of course, he''s just running\r\n32:23\r\nthrough everybody. Then slides to 50% in GM and then plummets to 46% in\r\n32:29\r\nCelestial. Basically, this is a story of punishment. Low elo doesn''t know what to do with him even before the bug. And\r\n32:35\r\nthen higher elo is used to his shenanigans. A lot of the players that climbed from low elo to mid elo to maybe\r\n32:43\r\neven celestial on Black Panther now suddenly find themselves in a position where their [ __ ] don''t work no more.\r\n32:49\r\nThose players peel, they counter, they swap in many cases and then he just collapses. The higher you go, the harder\r\n32:57\r\nhe falls. Next up, we have Human Torch. Interesting. He is a quiet climber and a\r\nHuman Torch\r\n33:04\r\nbit of a sleeper pick this season. 50 to 55% through the low ranks, then 53% in\r\n33:10\r\nGM, and then 56% in celestial. I always found them to have an awkward weird kit\r\n33:16\r\nthat low elo avoids, and then better players eventually make it work. Typically, when a hero that people find\r\n33:23\r\nannoying to pilot climbs like this, i