character is bad. It\r\n37:10\r\njust means that he is probably more punishable than others and that reflects in the win rate. Next up, we have Elsa\r\nElsa Bloodstone\r\n37:16\r\nBloodstone and she is also quite flat. I mean, well, she''s not, you''ve seen her, she''s not completely flat, but in terms\r\n37:22\r\nof win rate, it''s around 50%. 47 to 51% through the low ranks and then 50% in\r\n37:28\r\nboth GM and celestial. It sort of makes sense. This is your typical do everything flex DPS that lands right at\r\n37:36\r\nthe median line because she''s never really specialized enough to spike at anything specific. She peels, she can\r\n37:42\r\nzone a little bit, she can run anti-dive, just a bit of everything, but a master of none. She is a perfectly\r\n37:49\r\nrespectable utility pick that will fill a DPS role if that''s what you want to\r\nNamor\r\n37:54\r\nplay. Next up, we have Neore. Now he is fine low and then sinks high which is\r\n38:00\r\nreally depressing to see. 48 to 50% through the low ranks, 47% in\r\n38:05\r\nGrandmaster and then 43% the celestial. Yuck. Maybe maybe one of the reasons why\r\n38:11\r\nhis win rate sinks at the top is because he has deployables and those deployables get destroyed very quickly by the higher\r\n38:19\r\nranked players. What reads as area denial in bronze and oh my god the squids. I''m dying to the squids becomes\r\n38:26\r\na really minor inconvenience in Celestial unless you''re very creative and purposeful with how you play them\r\n38:32\r\nmore. So, I think we''ll see how the data changes week over week, but I think this falling line is just smart players\r\n38:39\r\nrouting around his entire problem by just shooting at him. Next up, we have the Punisher. And this one really\r\nThe Punisher\r\n38:45\r\nsurprised me. I mean, he sits behind the tanks and shoots. And then he has the really cool team up where he can shoot a\r\n38:52\r\nlot more and faster. But he is about 48% at every rank. Low and high, it doesn''t\r\